      "message": "test(sim): bridge the uncut gap under the overhang laws' rapid\n\nrapid_under's two floor slots along X 17 stop at Y +-8.5, so the\njudged rapid's disc X [14, 20] crossed Y (-5.5, 5.5) uncut to the stock\ntop (Z 20). Its three old column samples stood in the slots; the gap\nwas silent only because the rapid was never marched (#140). The march\nconvicts it correctly: the rapid at Z 5 or 12.5 really drives through\nstock, ledge or not, model or not. The fixture was wrong, not rapids.rs.\n\nThe gap is now bridged before the rapid: a floor pass along X 18 (disc\nX [15, 21], stops at the ledge's edge) and a pass above the ledge at\nZ 12.5 along X 17. What stands in the footprint is the strip X [14, 15)\nunder Z 12.5, the hidden band under the ledge: the rapid under the\nledge is still convicted, the rapid above it is clean. The bare-post and\nno-model tests judge rapid_cleared, the same program with the floor\nbridge along X 17, which clears the strip. Beside a bare post the strip\nis open from above and rapid_under still convicts there (a real\ncollision), so no single program can be clean beside the post and\nconvicted under the ledge once the rapid is marched. The doc comment no\nlonger claims three samples are enough.\n\nFixes #202\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
